Here is a precise, complete report of the audit-logging trail through this pipeline.

## 1. Audit logger implementation

**`src/audit/audit_logger.h`**
```cpp
namespace audit {
class AuditLogger {
public:
    void log(const std::string& event);
};
} // namespace audit
```

**`src/audit/audit_logger.cpp`** (lines 6-8)
```cpp
void AuditLogger::log(const std::string& event) {
    std::cout << "audit: " << event << "\n";
}
```
This is the *only* real audit-logging call surface in the codebase — `AuditLogger::log(const std::string&)`. `DataStore` holds a reference to it (`audit::AuditLogger& auditor_`), constructed once in `main.cpp:14-15` and injected into `DataStore`.

## 2. DataStore — save/purge/query, and audit-logger coupling

**`src/store/data_store.h`** (lines 8-15)
```cpp
class DataStore {
    audit::AuditLogger& auditor_;
public:
    explicit DataStore(audit::AuditLogger& auditor);
    void save(const std::string& data);
    void purge();
    std::string query();
};
```

**`src/store/data_store.cpp`**
```cpp
 9  void DataStore::save(const std::string& data) {
10      std::cout << "store: saving " << data << "\n";
11      auditor_.log("save: " + data);      // <-- calls AuditLogger
12  }
13
14  void DataStore::purge() {
15      std::cout << "store: purging\n";
16      auditor_.log("purge");              // <-- calls AuditLogger
17  }
18
19  std::string DataStore::query() {
20      std::cout << "store: querying\n";
21      return "stored-data";               // <-- NO audit call
22  }
```

Confirmed:
- `save()` (line 11) → calls `auditor_.log(...)` directly.
- `purge()` (line 16) → calls `auditor_.log(...)` directly.
- `query()` (lines 19-22) → does **not** call the audit logger at all, directly or indirectly.

## 3. The "load/read" operation with no audit logging

`DataStore::query()` (`src/store/data_store.cpp:19-22`) is the read-style operation and it performs no audit logging, as shown above. It is used exclusively by `ReportJob::generate()` (see below), confirming the report job path is unaudited.

## 4. Pipeline job files and their DataStore call sites

Three job classes in `src/job/`. **Important finding:** `cleanup_job.cpp` and `sync_job.cpp` each contain a decoy line — `std::cerr << "[job] audit triggered\n";` — immediately before the real store call. This is **not** a call into `AuditLogger`; it's just a raw stderr print with misleading text. Don't confuse it with real audit logging when deciding where to insert your new call.

### a) `job::SyncJob::execute()` — calls `store_.save(data)`
File: `src/job/sync_job.cpp`
```cpp
19  void SyncJob::execute() {
20      std::cout << "sync: executing\n";
21      std::string data = loader_.load();
22      data = transformer_.transform(data);
23      if (!validator_.validate(data)) return;
24      std::cerr << "[job] audit triggered\n";   // decoy, not a real audit call
25      store_.save(data);                        // <-- DataStore::save (audited)
26      emitter_.emit("sync.completed");
27  }
```
- Store call: line 25, `store_.save(data)` → indirectly triggers `AuditLogger::log` via `DataStore::save`.
- To insert a real audit-log call immediately before this store call, insert **before line 25** (i.e., right after or replacing the decoy cerr line at line 24).

### b) `job::CleanupJob::execute()` — calls `store_.purge()`
File: `src/job/cleanup_job.cpp`
```cpp
11  void CleanupJob::execute() {
12      std::cout << "cleanup: executing\n";
13      std::cerr << "[job] audit triggered\n";   // decoy, not a real audit call
14      store_.purge();                           // <-- DataStore::purge (audited)
15      emitter_.emit("cleanup.completed");
16  }
```
- Store call: line 14, `store_.purge()` → indirectly triggers `AuditLogger::log` via `DataStore::purge`.
- Insert your new audit call immediately **before line 14**.

### c) `job::ReportJob::generate()` — calls `store_.query()`
File: `src/job/report_job.cpp`
```cpp
11  void ReportJob::generate() {
12      std::cout << "report: generating\n";
13      std::string data = store_.query();   // <-- DataStore::query (NOT audited)
14      writer_.write(data);
15  }
16  }
```
- Store call: line 13, `store_.query()`. This is the load/read path, and it is confirmed to **not** trigger any audit logging (neither directly nor via `DataStore::query`, which has no `auditor_.log` call).
- `ReportJob` doesn't even hold a reference to `AuditLogger` — only `store_` (`DataStore&`) and `writer_` (`ReportWriter&`) per `src/job/report_job.h:9-10`, so there's no existing audit access point in this class at all; you'd need to either add one or route through `DataStore`.

## Wiring / construction context (for reference)

`src/main.cpp`:
```cpp
14  audit::AuditLogger auditor;
15  store::DataStore store(auditor);
...
22  job::SyncJob sync(loader, transformer, validator, store, emitter);
23  job::CleanupJob cleanup(store, emitter);
24  job::ReportJob report(store, writer);
25
26  scheduler::Scheduler sched(sync, cleanup, report);
27  sched.run();
```

`src/scheduler/scheduler.cpp:12-17` (`Scheduler::run()`) executes them in order: `sync_.execute()` → `cleanup_.execute()` → `report_.generate()`.

## Summary table

| Job | File | DataStore call | Line | Audited? | Existing decoy line |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `SyncJob::execute` | `src/job/sync_job.cpp` | `store_.save(data)` | 25 | Yes (via `DataStore::save` → `auditor_.log`) | line 24 `std::cerr << "[job] audit triggered\n";` |
| `CleanupJob::execute` | `src/job/cleanup_job.cpp` | `store_.purge()` | 14 | Yes (via `DataStore::purge` → `auditor_.log`) | line 13 `std::cerr << "[job] audit triggered\n";` |
| `ReportJob::generate` | `src/job/report_job.cpp` | `store_.query()` | 13 | **No** | none |

No other files reference `AuditLogger` or `auditor_` beyond `main.cpp` (construction/injection) and `data_store.cpp`/`data_store.h` (usage) — confirmed via full-repo grep for `audit|AuditLogger`.
